From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:40:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] docs: env_switches row for DM_NVN_BC_ALIAS

Upstream a631295b reads DM_NVN_BC_ALIAS in nvn_mtl.m without a row in
docs/env_switches.tsv, so dm/tools/tests/test_env_switches.py fails on seedds/nxnative main.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: the env switch table test needs a row with a meaning for every switch the code reads

Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#976

---
 docs/env_switches.tsv | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/docs/env_switches.tsv b/docs/env_switches.tsv
index 6c08a73..0ccdbfe 100644
--- a/docs/env_switches.tsv
+++ b/docs/env_switches.tsv
@@ -123,6 +123,7 @@ DM_NRO_DIR	path	folder of NROs the shader split reads like `main`, and in which
 DM_NVN_ALLOCPROF	diagnostic	`=1` charges Metal allocation growth to each replayed op type and function, and logs command allocator sizes and each new texture (serial, size, format, storage); `=2` also gives each main submission a fresh command allocator and reports command memory by operation, by encoder, by submission size and the indirect-count multi-draws encoded
 DM_NVN_API	switch	`=<major>.<minor>` overrides the NVN API version `nvnDeviceGetInteger` reports (by default decided by the SDK version or the profile's `device_api`: 55.15 for SDK 11 and later, 53.313 before)
 DM_NVN_BARRIER	switch	How draw passes are ordered: `full` (default) waits for all earlier GPU work, `game` only for the previous pass's fragment stage unless the game set a barrier, `ab` alternates with the `DM_AB` phases
+DM_NVN_BC_ALIAS	diagnostic	`0` sends a texture copy into an uncompressed alias of a compressed texture to the alias itself, as before the copy wrote the compressed texture (the default)
 DM_NVN_BF_WANT	path	`=<file>`: appends the key of each fragment shader whose passes could not be merged for lack of a readable-tile version to that file, once per key
 DM_NVN_BLIT_ORDER	diagnostic	`0` drops the barriers between dependent operations in the copy encoder, which reproduces the fountain's vertical stripes in Mario Wonder
 DM_NVN_CAPTURE	diagnostic	`=<frame>:1:<path>` writes that frame (from its first submit to its present) to one file: pool bytes, registries, program keys, the textures whose content lives only in Metal, each submission's records with pointers relocatable, and the presented frame's SHA-256 and pixels; `dm/gfx/tests/nvn_replay` replays it ([development.md](development.md#frame-capture-and-replay))
